    "body": "Hi @flw-cn, sorry for the delay on the review.\r\n\r\nRight now, the biggest blocker to merging is that when I check out your commit in git locally, the parent information is invalid. Git thinks that this commit is its own parent, which makes it impossible to do operations like merge/rebase or diffs. This will definitely need to be fixed before we can merge this, because right now, I can't tell if the automated checks are working correctly due to this commit having no parent and no shared history with the rest of starship.\r\n\r\nTBH, I'm not entirely sure how to fix this--you might be able to cherry-pick these commits onto the latest copy of master, or you might have to make a patch and apply it over the top, since git is doing something weird. Once that's fixed, I can take another look at this.\r\n\r\n(I've also left some review comments down below, but the biggest blocker right now is this git history issue).",
